ombination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in reduced row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{4}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=8{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{4}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th) and ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable corresponding to the non-pivot column. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433965 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433963 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433965 1069 "q-74999" 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433965 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433965 1071 "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433965 1072 #uuid "64b2528a-be45-5f89-bf42-907c121c9d08" 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433965 1074 "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd) and ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable corresponding to the non-pivot column. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433966 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433968 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433966 1062 #uuid "34826f51-bff5-576f-8e59-d94eb0f524b1" 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433966 1063 #edb/ref 17592186433965 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433967 1062 #uuid "54aec285-4fb2-5f72-9458-615e815400c0" 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433967 1063 #edb/ref 17592186433964 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433968 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433967 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433968 1062 #uuid "8b0318dc-2ed5-55c8-99e2-ef561cb961f3" 13194139534720 17592186045417 true] [17592186433968 1063 #edb/ref 17592186345022 13194139534720 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-4586137b-2f21-5dd9-9f92-f73895c531d1" 17592186433946 "answer-038d8f66-0fdf-5eca-b0da-b68e8724c6db" 17592186433947 "answer-11fe67bf-961a-57c3-a494-79893e59e352" 17592186433948 "answer-3634eb4a-2da6-506c-862a-4df1259f8573" 17592186433949 "answer-3bfcd48e-1e57-5c21-853e-08ad7ac4a5f7" 17592186433950 "answer-664c9ed3-862f-5378-872f-f842ae26bbab" 17592186433951 "answer-72404e91-0b79-5fbe-bf3b-a415c48e7a